  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So, the Steam client has stopped working with opencomposite.\nIt didn't give any errors, so there was no way to diagnose the issue.\nThat is, until I looked in the plugins and saw that the Oculus dlls were there.\nAs it is, -vrmode oculus opens SteamVR\nThe ovr dlls conflict with OpenComposite.\nSo, -vrmode oculus is not an option, and opencomposite isn't either.\nEither get rid of the ovr dlls if you're not going to use them, or let us use -vrmode oculus without running steamvr.\nThe Oculus store version is not an option for most people because oftentimes you don't see other players in the same room due to version mismatches, because the oculus store is a buggy mess that refuses to actually properly install games half the time, and because some people have modified their Oculus client to be offline, preventing downloading and upkeep of VRChat on the platform.\nPlease do something about this, this is exacerbating.\nThere is no reason to lock functionality to specific platforms.",
